## Architecture

The project follows a **Medallion Architecture** implemented using **Microsoft Fabric**.

```mermaid
flowchart LR

    %% Source Systems
    A[Orders<br/>CSV]
    B[Returns<br/>Excel]
    C[Inventory<br/>JSON]

    %% Ingestion
    D[Microsoft Fabric<br/>Data Pipeline<br/>Copy Data]

    %% Medallion Layers
    E[Bronze Layer<br/>Raw Data]
    F[Silver Layer<br/>Cleaned & Validated Data]
    G[Gold Layer<br/>Business KPIs]

    %% Processing
    P[PySpark<br/>Data Cleaning & Transformation]
    I[Data Integration<br/>Orders + Returns + Inventory]
    K[Product + Month<br/>KPI Aggregation]

    %% Analytics
    H[Power BI<br/>Analytics Dashboard]

    %% Flow
    A --> D
    B --> D
    C --> D

    D --> E

    E --> P
    P --> F

    F --> I
    I --> K
    K --> G

    G --> H



### This will render roughly like:

**Orders (CSV)** ─┐  
**Returns (Excel)** ──→ **Fabric Data Pipeline** → **Bronze** → **PySpark** → **Silver** → **Integration** → **Gold KPIs** → **Power BI**  
**Inventory (JSON)** ─┘

The important part is that you **paste the whole block**, including both sets of triple backticks. GitHub will automatically render the `mermaid` section as a graphical architecture diagram rather than showing the text/code.
